---
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import DesignHead from "../../components/DesignHead.astro";
import Analytics from "../../components/Analytics.astro";
import HardwareAffiliateCTA from "../../components/HardwareAffiliateCTA.astro";

const TITLE = "SDG&E Battery Storage ROI Guide 2026: Rates & Economics";
const DESCRIPTION = "San Diego Gas & Electric (SDG&E) battery payback breakdown under NEM 3.0 rules and EV-TOU-5 rate schedules.";
const CANONICAL_URL = "https://mygridpermit.com/blog/sdge-battery-roi-guide/";
const HEADLINE = "San Diego Solar & Battery Economics: SDG&E Rate Analysis (2026)";

// No datePublished/dateModified/image: not stated with real precision on
// this page, and no real hero image asset exists for this post.
const articleSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Article",
	headline: HEADLINE,
	description: DESCRIPTION,
	mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": CANONICAL_URL },
	author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "GridPermit" },
	publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "GridPermit" },
};
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
<head>
	<Analytics />
	<DesignHead />
	<meta charset="UTF-8">
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
	<title>{TITLE}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
	<link rel="canonical" href={CANONICAL_URL} />
	<meta property="og:type" content="article" />
	<meta property="og:url" content={CANONICAL_URL} />
	<meta property="og:title" content={TITLE} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
	<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={TITLE} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
	<meta name="google-site-verification" content="b36wwqlXise5bGI8ckWqbybnEoCYlsTmp4BiV" />
	<link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap-index.xml" />

	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
</head>
<body data-track-view="blog_article_viewed">
	<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
	<Header />
	<main class="article-container" id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
		<span class="article-category">Regional Analysis</span>
		<h1>{HEADLINE}</h1>
		<p class="article-meta">Check your current tariff before comparing quotes.</p>

		<p class="lead-paragraph">Thinking about adding a battery to an existing solar system? Start with your SDG&E bill, the system's interconnection agreement and a written retrofit proposal. This page sets out the inputs to check; it does not calculate a guaranteed payback or promise a particular saving.</p>

		<h2>1. Read your exact tariff</h2>
		<p>Use the rate schedule on your current bill rather than an example peak price. Compare import prices, export compensation, fixed charges and the hours when you use electricity. SDG&E explains how its <a href="https://www.sdge.com/residential/pricing-plans/about-our-pricing-plans/time-use-plans" rel="noopener noreferrer">Time-of-Use plans</a> work and how the <a href="https://www.sdge.com/electric-billing" rel="noopener noreferrer">Base Services Charge</a> appears on bills. A battery proposal should show the tariff assumptions it uses.</p>

		<h2>2. Compare the complete retrofit proposal</h2>
		<p>Ask for the installed price, usable battery capacity, output power, reserve settings, warranty, compatibility with your existing solar equipment, and any permitting or electrical work included in the quote. Ask the provider to explain how the proposed operating settings fit your existing interconnection agreement. Keep backup capability separate from projected bill reductions when comparing proposals.</p>

		<HardwareAffiliateCTA productLabel="Battery and backup-power products" state="CA" city="San Diego" />

		<h2>3. Scope and next step</h2>
		<p>The referral option above is limited to homeowners in the City of San Diego served by SDG&E who already have solar. Confirm all three conditions before continuing. For another city, use our <a href="/california/utility/sdg-e/">verified SDG&E city guides</a>; this page does not imply that every city or project is eligible.</p>
		<p class="related-guides-nav">Looking for the local permit process specifically in Poway or Vista? See the GridPermit guides for <a href="/california/poway/solar-permit-guide/">Poway</a> and <a href="/california/vista/solar-permit-guide/">Vista</a>.</p>
		<p class="sources-text">Method: compare your actual bill and written proposal, not a generic peak-price spread or promised payback period. The linked SDG&E pages are the primary references for billing-plan structure. GridPermit does not determine your system's compatibility, final price, financing terms or project approval.</p>
		<div class="cta-banner"><h3>Check your local permit path</h3><a href="/california/san-diego/solar-permit-guide/" class="btn-banner-cta">Read the San Diego permit guide →</a></div>

	</main>
	<Footer />
	<style>
		.article-container { max-width: 820px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }.article-category { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); text-transform: uppercase; }.article-meta { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--gp-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem; }.lead-paragraph { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--gp-ink); }.sources-text { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--gp-muted); background: var(--gp-surface); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 2px; margin-top: 2rem; line-height: 1.5; }.related-guides-nav { font-size: 0.9rem; }.cta-banner { background: var(--gp-surface); color: var(--gp-ink); padding: 2.5rem; border-radius: 2px; text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem; }.btn-banner-cta { background: var(--gp-accent); color: var(--gp-ink); padding: 0.85rem 1.75rem; border-radius: 2px; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin-top: 1rem; }
	</style>
</body>
</html>
